  VI. ELLIPTIC CURVES AND THE CAYLEY FRAME
  --------------------------------------------------

  An elliptic curve E over Q has CONDUCTOR N = prod p^{f_p}.
  Conductor 42 = 2*3*7 means BAD REDUCTION at exactly {2,3,7}.
  The three Hurwitz primes are EXACTLY the bad primes of E.

